s water treatment and process applications, and cleaning and sanitizing solutions to manufacturing, food and beverage processing, transportation, chemical, primary metals and mining, power generation, global refining, petrochemical, pulp and paper industries. The Global Institutional & Specialty segment provides cleaning and sanitizing products to the foodservice, healthcare, hospitality, lodging, government, education and retail industries. The Global Pest Elimination segment provides pest elimination services to detect, prevent, and eliminate pests comprising rodents and insects in full-service and quick-service restaurants, food and beverage processors, hotels, grocery operations, and other commercial segments, including education, life sciences, and healthcare. The Global Life Sciences segment provides cleaning and contamination control solutions to pharmaceutical and personal care manufacturers. It offers its products under the Ecolab, Kay, Purolite, and Bioquell brand names. The company sells its products through field sales and corporate account personnel, distributors, and dealers. Ecolab Inc. was founded in 1923 and is headquartered in Saint Paul, Minnesota.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christophe  Beck | CEO, President & Chairman of the Board | Age 57 | Compensation: $5.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 48K people. Revenue per employee of $335K ranks in the bottom quartile among Basic Materials peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $40K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Ecolab Inc. is a large-cap basic materials business with a $86.7B market cap on $16.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $1.9B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 12 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.42\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 8.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.8%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 218% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 3 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.1831575463588675},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $6.0M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-6030207.54},{"text":"Significant goodwill (37% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Investment Analysts\u2019 Upgrades for November 13th (ADSK, DAVE, DPZ, DTM, ECL, ENGN, LFTO, NMAX, NMG)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/investment-analysts-upgrades-for-november-13th-adsk-dave-dpz-dtm-ecl-engn-lfto-nmax-nmg.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794595487.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.856,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Ecolab (ECL), What Is Drawing Fresh Attention To The Stock?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-ecl/ecolab/news/ecolab-ecl-what-is-drawing-fresh-attention-to-the-stock","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794545062.286,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.913,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Neo Performance Materials (OTCMKTS:NOPMF) & Ecolab (NYSE:ECL) Critical Analysis","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/neo-performance-materials-otcmktsnopmf-ecolab-nyseecl-critical-analysis.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794431704.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.914,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Ecolab upgraded at Wells Fargo, touting CoolIT and Ovivo acquisitions","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4672596-ecolab-upgraded-at-wells-fargo-touting-coolit-and-ovivo-acquisitions","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794599003.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":1,"scope":"company","t